<snip>

Single bus or split bus mode is not determined by the personality 
module. The backplane is set up for split bus mode, and at the rear side 
of disk slot 6 there is either a terminator module BA35X-ME (for split 
bus mode) or a jumper module BA35X-MF (for single bus mode). The unused 
module is "parked" in an empty space behind disk slot 1. (Some documents 
say that only the jumper module can be parked, I'm not sure how relevant 
this is).

To access (and swap) these modules, you need to remove the fans on the 
rear side of the BA356.

More details are available on <http://labs.hoffmanlabs.com/node/54>.

An explanation of the switches on the personaliry module can be found in 
an attachment of this ITRC forum thread:
<http://forums13.itrc.hp.com/service/forums/questionanswer.do?threadId=
916593>
(thanks to Hein van den Heuvel).

Regards,
Hans.


