shelf/disk/controller/cable works with VMS.  (I had been using a 20 MB/s
grey BA356 with a personality module with the (physically) wide 68-pin
connector on the side (which requires a rather rare cable), the disks
being a mixture of 10, 20 and 40 MB/s.  However, performance was flaky,
probably because I had to use either a too long cable (presumably
intended for LVD operation, where the cable length is not such a
problem) or an adapter since the cable connecting to the personality 
module ended in the physically narrow 68-pin plug and I need the 
physically wide one for the PWS.  But with the new personality module 
(with two physically narrow 68-pin connectors on the front) came a cable 
connecting these to a physically wide 68-pin connector.)
 


