>> RA-81.
>
> I agree. I ran an ra60 drive for a while on an 82xx series bi bus
> machine. Around 4 to 500 watts spun up for just 205 Mbytes. Great drive
> in some ways though, Sounded like an aircraft taking off as it spun up
> and shifted *serious* amounts of air when running :-).
>
> Still have a load of RA60 packs in the loft, but not much chance of
> reading them now. Have enough hardware to build a machine, but haven't
> seen an ra60 for sale in 10 years or more, even on Ebay. Sad, but would
