RA60 drives were a wonder of modernity, silence and frugal power 
requirements compared to older stuff like RP06, or RM03. The RM03 really 
sounded like a jet aeroplane when it spun up... I don't even dare think 
of the power requirements of the RP06...

And capacity was likewise not impressive by today. The RM03 held a 
whopping 67MB, while the RP06 held a while 176MB (if I remember right, 
that is...).

The RA60 is tricky, though. My experience with them is that by now, 
drives normally refuse to read the packs because of tight media checking 
and advanced algorithms in use. Older drives are much more forgiving 
(and stupid).

But "modern" RA drives have much higher capacity, smaller form factor, 
and lower power requirements. The RA60 were among the first RA drives 
ever produced, and the only one ever with a removable pack.

	Johnny

