Well, the same source, compiled with different overlay structures - is 
that the same image? After all, all the binary executable as well as 
data, is the same, but loaded in different places, and with calls to the 
overlay loader sprinkled differently...

I don't know how overlaid binaries looks on RT-11, but I bet there must 
be some kind of information in the binary header telling which parts to 
load at image activation, and which ones that should be untouched at 
that point. And the overlay loader must have a mapping table to help it 
read the proper parts from disk at a later point, and know where to 
write those parts to in memory.
While the latter part can be placed in the image itself, the original 
loading must exclude (possibly a large) part of the file from actually 
loading at activation.

	Johnny



