Asking prices on eBay depend on who's selling. Some companies, like
ELI offer refurbished or modified and improved gear and that's not
cheap.
In the Netherlands we've got a thing like www.marktplaats.nl which is
also a kind of auction site. Kind of because it organised the Dutch
way,
hardly any rules and compared to eBay it is chaotic. Sometimes DEC
gear is offered for sale.

Gear that comes out of a computer room is usually in very good
cosmetic condition. Be aware that it wasn't turned off at all or
incidentally.
So disks and fans may not readily start up when the systems has been
powered off for some time.

Two of my daughters now live in their own home and one bedroom was
converted to conputerroom. The attic is the main computerroom
and my study has two alpha's and a pc.
My main problems are heat and the electricity bill. Alpha Servers
1000/1200 etc not really switch off, their power supplies remain
connected to
the mains and with this number of systems the electricity bill
steadily increases. I still wonder why the police hasn't suspected
that I'm growing
marihuana or so ;-)
Phillip's threads keep us on the right track: this is a VMS newsgroup
not a bash-Bill or aniti-unix group...
Hans


