Hans Vlems <hvlems@freenet.de> writes: 

> In the Netherlands we've got a thing like www.marktplaats.nl which is
> also a kind of auction site. Kind of because it organised the Dutch
> way,
> hardly any rules and compared to eBay it is chaotic. Sometimes DEC
> gear is offered for sale.

But probably it is not an actual "Dutch auction".  (In English, this 
usually means a reverse option, where the starting price is high and 
drops until someone agrees to buy.  I think the rules for the actual 
Dutch auction (traditionally and AFAIK still used when selling flower 
bulbs etc) are somewhat more complicated.

> Two of my daughters now live in their own home and one bedroom was
> converted to conputerroom. The attic is the main computerroom
> and my study has two alpha's and a pc.

> My main problems are heat and the electricity bill. 

Having the computer room in the cellar is good since the heat rises, so
in the winter you can save on other heating costs.  (Of course, it's
still cheaper to heat with gas or oil than with electricity.)  In the
summer, it is cooler so the fans can run at a lower speed.  In the
attic, the heat is wasted in the winter and in the summer the fans will 
run at higher speed, or it might be too hot to run things at all.

> Alpha Servers
> 1000/1200 etc not really switch off, their power supplies remain
> connected to
> the mains and with this number of systems the electricity bill
> steadily increases. 

Yes.  This is true of many appliances as well, but the ALPHA servers 
seem to draw a lot of current even when in standby.  For such machines, 
I connect them to a row of plugs on an extension cord which I can switch 
off.

> I still wonder why the police hasn't suspected
> that I'm growing
> marihuana or so ;-)

There was actually someone arrested (I don't recall where) recently for 
this.  He was investigated because of the high electricity bill, which 
was used for illuminating the plants.



