> consumption problem. =A0Why don't you put them on separate breakers or
> even large power distribution boxes that you can buy in any consumer/
> home electronics, self-services, etc. store?

No three-phase because it doesn't give you more power per phase. All
the equipment is single phase
and set for 220 Volts (though actual mains output is now at the
European 230V standard).
The systems are behind two fuses, 16 A each. So there's 3500 W
available per fuse; assuming a near
perfect resistive load, which the Alpha's and VAXes are. Sufficient to
power them all.
