Are you looking for different answers than the ones you got when you
asked similar sounding questions on December 19 last year or March 22
this year? ;)

Partial summary of those discussions (from memory):
. readers are not telepathic

. part numbers are helpful

. definitive answers pretty much require definitive part numbers

. older monitors that are fixed frequency likely require sync on green
if 3BNC and are rarely compatible with VGA graphics cards - iirc,
exceptions include the TGA-based cards such as the ZLXp-E* series
which can be configured to produce sync-on-green.

Iirc, VRC16s can be handy in these circumstances too as they do sync
on green or VGA or 5BNC, and are available under a variety of
different names not just from DEC as VRC16.


