Many/most of the older flat screens could display resolutions less than 
their native resolution 1:1 (of course, with a black frame around the 
picture). This results in excellent quality of the display at the price 
of not using the whole real estate the monitor offers, but imho is the 
better solution.

For newer (especially cheap) monitors this feature has mostly been taken 
away; some offer to display the picture in the right aspect ratio, but 
this is not enough. Before purchasing a (now or used) LCD monitor, check 
out the specs or documentation whether it is capable of displaying non-
native resolutions 1:1.

Hans.


