I know how to get to the VMS SRM console on a PWS: F2, then CMOS setup,
then F6 for advanced setup, then select OpenVMS SRM console, then F10 to
save, then F10 to save again, then reset button.  I've done this a few
times on machines with bad batteries and/or with a new (to me) machine
which previously didn't run VMS.  It has always worked.  (To be sure, I 
didn't try it on machines with good batteries which were already set to 
the VMS console.)  Today, a new (to me) PWS always returns to the WNT 
console.  (Interestingly, I noticed that when one selects the console in 
the advanced CMOS setup, it says the settings will be displayed after 
the next power cycle.  Reset has always worked for me, and if a power 
cycle were necessary this wouldn't work at all with a dead battery.  
Nevertheless, I tried a power cycle and the result is the same.)

The machine is a PWS 433au.  Could such a thing exist but somehow not 
support the VMS console?



