>Is it possible to connect a VGA graphics card (e.g. those in newer
>ALPHAs) to a monitor with BNC RGB inputs (e.g. those used with 
>VAXstations and older ALPHAs)?  I have one such cable, but it is known 
>to be defective.  I have some cables which are RGBBW; connecting up just 
>the RGB inputs (which is all the monitor has) results in a signal being 
>displayed, but it is extremely noisy and not at all useful.

Well, fix the bad cable, then.

The PC world uses monitors that synch to the rate of the video source.
The rest of the world used to use video outputs that set the rate of the
video source to match the monitor.

So if you plug your DEC monitor into a PC, the PC will have no way of knowing
what rate to drive the monitor at, whether to supply synch on green, or any
of that stuff.  So you will have to set it by hand.
--scott
