As others have said, get a new battery.  There are three stages here:

1. Battery dying, ut will keep the settings across a power cycle
2. Battery not fully dead; you can get away with a reset
3. Battery so dead that it won't keep the settings across a reset

The bit of my answer you snipped:

> This has got me out of several jams when a battery has died and the 
> shops are shut.

By which I meant get a battery before your next power cycle.

