On the PWSs the default boot console is the ARC console.
When the battery goes dead, it defaults to ARC and switching to SRM 
doesn't work because it requires battery voltage to save the change.

I suspect on your 2100 it's defaulting to a serial console rather than 
the local video.
Does the 2100 even have a replaceable battery on the motherboard?

